    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Paleoclimatology",
    "problem": "A lack of continuous, high-resolution atmospheric methane records beyond 650,000 years has limited the understanding of long-term external forcings and internal feedbacks, which are essential for predicting the methane budget in a future warmer climate.",
    "method": "We present a detailed 800,000-year atmospheric methane record from the EPICA Dome C ice core and use spectral analysis to identify the orbital and millennial-scale features controlling its long-term variability, linking them to changes in tropical sources and global ice volume.",
    "task": "The task is to reconstruct and analyze an 800,000-year atmospheric methane record from an Antarctic ice core to identify the orbital and millennial-scale factors that controlled its concentration and variability in the past.",
