            "target_entity_instance": "CH4",
            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "The air from polar ice-core samples of about 40 g (Bern) and 50 g (LGGE) is extracted with a melt-refreezing method under vacuum, and the extracted gas is then analysed for CH4 by gas chromatography. Two standard gases (408 p.p.b.v. CH4, 1,050 p.p.b.v. CH4) were used at Bern and one (499 p.p.b.v. CH4) at LGGE, to calibrate the gas chromatographs.",
